      "correctness": 9,
      "severity": 8,
      "profitability": 8
    },
    {
      "function_name": "mintReservedTokens",
      "vulnerability": "Missing total-supply cap for reserve minting",
      "criticism": "The reasoning is correct. mintReservedTokens checks only quantity <= reserve and then decrements reserve; it never enforces totalSupply() + quantity <= maxsupply. Since setReserve can reset reserve repeatedly, the owner can call setReserve(maxsupply) and mintReservedTokens(maxsupply) multiple times, minting unbounded tokens despite the advertised cap. This is a real supply-cap violation and a severe centralization risk. The key limitation is that the function is onlyOwner, so an unprivileged external attacker cannot trigger it unless the owner key is malicious or compromised. Following the usual treatment of owner-only minting as an admin trust issue, profitability for an external attacker is low. This issue is also closely related to the mutable reserve logic in setReserve.",
